# Keep non-runtime files out of Vercel deployments to reduce Deployment Storage.
# Verified 2026-09-16: none of these are imported by the Next.js app or its
# build. The Python renderer (tools/eeg-render) is a separate Moltbot worker —
# the app only references the Supabase rows it writes, never the Python source.
# design-assets/ is a logo archive (~9 MB, incl. a 5.8 MB Test_Logo.png),
# docs/ are the EEG Atlas planning notes, backups/ and homelab/ are reference.
#
# NOTE: public/ (served static assets, incl. the ~35 MB question-bank PNGs),
# src/, content/qbank/ (traced into functions), scripts/ (run in prebuild) and
# supabase/ are all required and stay in the deployment.
design-assets
tools
docs
backups
homelab
